            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0833" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/578: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-05T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 5—9:37
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. The Chinese Government urges reply to its note of February 27th, transmitted
                    by Legation April 7th.<anchor n="84" xml:id="d764-f1"/> I request authorization
                    to reply in the sense of British recommendation quoted in the Legation despatch
                    number 3207 or if Department prefers to assent to immediate 5 per cent revision
                    and increase with abolition of likin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
